 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\n\nConsumption 20    80   100        ?  kWh\n|_|}\nMR Reason \u00a3E     Z    T        T\n\n08                   02                01                               01\n\n60%        20%           100%\nWeighting Por. |--------------- |------------- |------------------------ |--------\n\nExample: Basis for Extrapolation\n\nThe period from O01 to O2 is not representative because it does not have the minimum weighting portion (only 20% rather than the\nrequired 50%). This means that this period alone cannot be used as a basis for extrapolation. The system goes back to the next\nmeter reading (08). The period from O1 to 08 is representative because it has a weighting portion of 20% + 60% = 80%. The\nperiod from 01 to 08 can be used as a basis for extrapolation.\n\nMeter Reading Results or Period Value as a Basis for Extrapolation\n\nThe system determines whether to use meter reading results or a selected period value as a basis for extrapolation in the following\nway:\n\nBased on the last correct meter reading results, the system goes back to the previous reading and runs through the following\nprocess:\n",
